Preamble

This license establishes the terms under which a given free software
Package may be copied, modified, distributed, and/or redistributed.
The intent is that the Copyright Holder maintains some artistic
control over the development of that Package while still keeping the
Package available as open source and free software.

You are always permitted to make arrangements wholly outside of this
license directly with the Copyright Holder of a given Package.  If the
terms of this license do not permit the full use that you propose to
make of the Package, you should contact the Copyright Holder and seek
a different licensing arrangement.

Definitions

    "Copyright Holder" means the individual(s) or organization(s)
    named in the copyright notice for the entire Package.

    "Contributor" means any party that has contributed code or other
    material to the Package, in accordance with the Copyright Holder's
    procedures.

    "You" and "your" means any person who would like to copy,
    distribute, or modify the Package.

    "Package" means the collection of files distributed by the
    Copyright Holder, and derivatives of that collection and/or
    of those files. A given Package may consist of either the Standard
    Version, or a Modified Version.

    "Distribute" means providing a copy of the Package or making it
    accessible to anyone else, or in the case of a company or
    organization, to others outside of your company or organization.

    "Distributor Fee" means any fee that you charge for Distributing
    this Package or providing support for this Package to another
    party.  It does not mean branding.

    "Standard Version" refers to the Package if it has not been
    modified, or has been modified only in ways explicitly requested
    by the Copyright Holder.

    "Modified Version" means the Package, when it has been changed,
    and such changes were not explicitly requested by the Copyright
    Holder.

    "Original License" means this Artistic License as Distributed with
    the Standard Version of the Package, in its current version or as
    it may be modified by The Perl Foundation in the future.

    "Source" form means the source code, documentation source, and
    configuration files for the Package.

    "Compiled" form means the compiled binary or object code or
    executable, including generated binary files, generated
    computer code, or translated or converted binary files.

    "Application" means the problem solving program, application, or
    other business function or application to which the Package is
    linked.

    "Aggregation" means a compilation of a number of separate
    independent programs, not based on the Package, which are
    not specifically written for the purpose of combining the Package
    with the independent programs.

    "Distribution" means the collection of files that constitute the
    Package as it is distributed by you.

    "Derivative Work" means any work derived from the Package,
    either through copyright or contract.

Permission for Use and Modification Without Distribution

(1)  You are permitted to use the Standard Version and create and use
Modified Versions for any purpose without restriction, provided that
you do not Distribute the Modified Version.

Permissions for Redistribution of the Standard Version

(2)  You may Distribute verbatim copies of the Source form of the
Standard Version of this Package in any medium without restriction,
either gratis or for a Distributor Fee, provided that you duplicate
all of the original copyright notices and associated disclaimers.  At
your discretion, such binary files may be included under the conditions
that you may Distribute them as provided in (3).

Permissions for Redistribution of Modified Versions of the Source
Form as a Standard Version

(3)  You may Distribute any Modified Version in Source form under the
conditions of section (2) above, provided that you include prominent
notices stating how and when you changed the Package, and provided that
the Modified Version is clearly distinguished from the Standard Version
in one of the following ways:

    (a)  make the Modified Version available as the Standard Version,
         with the Modified Version clearly named, so that the User
         can easily find the source of the Modified Version, and the
         Package name and version number are clearly present.

    (b)  make sure that the Modified Version has a different package
         name than the Standard Version.

    (c)  make sure that any non-Standard Version clearly carries a
         different version number or name from the Standard Version.

Permissions for Redistribution of Modified Versions of the Source
Form as a Non-Standard Version

(4)  You may Distribute any Modified Version in Source form without
distinguishing it from the Standard Version as required by section (3)
above, if you distribute the Modified Version exclusively in your own
organization or company, and do not distribute it to anyone outside your
organization or company.

Permissions for Redistribution of Non-Source Forms of Modified Versions

(5)  You may Distribute Non-Source Forms of a Modified Version
provided that you do the following with each Non-Source Form:

    (a)  do at least one of the following:

         (i)   make the Source form of the Modified Version available
               under the Original License, and include instructions on
               how to acquire the Source form from the Copyright Holder;

         (ii)  ensure that the Source form of the Modified Version is
               made available under the Original License as provided
               by the Copyright Holder;

         (iii) make the Source form available from the same place
               as the Non-Source Form;

    (b)  keep intact all copyright notices and disclaimers;

    (c)  clearly distinguish the Modified Version from the Standard
         Version.

Permissions for Aggregation

(6)  You may Aggregate the Package with other independent programs
and distribute the Aggregation provided that you do not state or imply
that the Package is your own, or that the Aggregation is your own.

Permissions for Linking

(7)  You may link the Package with other files to produce an
Application, and distribute the Application without restriction under
